  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers SLSA (Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts) v1.2 from OpenSSF: the Build track L0-L3 and Source track L1-L4 with their producer, build platform, organization and source control system requirements; the SLSA Provenance v1 predicate for in-toto attestations; distributing provenance; verifying artifacts against roots of trust and expectations; Verification Summary Attestations v1 and Source VSAs; and the threat model A-I. Version lines: SLSA v1.2 is current, v1.1, v1.0 and v0.1 are legacy, and the working draft (Build Environment and Dependency tracks) is tracked as a preview; Provenance and VSA predicates are separate families with v1 current and v0.2 and v0.1 legacy. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions, levels and tracks, provenance, verification, and threats.",
